  <title>Import a mail archive</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Data</gui><gui>Mail archive
  import</gui></guiseq> reads the messages in a Thunderbird mail file into
  <link xref="correspondence"/>. It is for mail the server no longer has,
  such as mail that was downloaded and removed from the server. Nothing is
  written to the file, and mail already in the database is left alone, so
  importing the same file twice does no harm.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Mail file</gui> with <gui>Browse</gui>, which
    starts in Thunderbird's own folder. A Thunderbird mail file has the name
    of its folder, such as <file>Inbox</file> or <file>Sent</file>, with no
    extension.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Call it</gui> is the folder name stored with each message.
    It starts as the file's name.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>These are messages this company sent</gui> for a Sent
    folder, so they count as sent rather than received.</p></item>
    <item><p>Leave <gui>File each message under the contact it was with</gui>
    checked to file received mail under whoever sent it, and sent mail under
    whoever it went to.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Look at the file</gui>. It counts the messages and
    gives the dates they cover, writing nothing, so you can tell it is the
    right file.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Import</gui>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>A large file takes a while; the bar shows how many messages have been
  read and stored. When it finishes it says how many were stored, how many
  were already there, how many were filed under a contact, and how many could
  not be. Closing the window stops the import; what was stored so far is
  kept, and importing the file again picks up the rest.</p>

  <p>Messages are matched to contacts by email address, the only thing an
  old message has to go on. An address belonging to more than one contact
  is filed under none of them, and deleted contacts are not matched.</p>

  <note><p>The correspondence window does not show the name given in
  <gui>Call it</gui> yet.</p></note>

</page>
